# Testing & quality

Catalog: [TESTING_SCENARIOS.md](../../TESTING_SCENARIOS.md) · CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml`

## Commands

```bash
npm test              # Jest (unit + integration)
npm run test:integration
npm run lint
npm run build         # next build + server tsc
npx tsc --project server/tsconfig.json
```

## Test layout

```
__tests__/
  unit/           # validation.test.ts, cacheInvalidation.test.ts
  integration/    # health, auth, tasks, projects, timeEntries
  setup.ts        # loads .env.test, sets JWT_SECRET
```

## Health tests

Use real handler from `server/health.ts` (`registerHealthRoute`, `buildHealthPayload`) — mock `testConnection` / Redis, not a fake endpoint.

## Auth tests

Supertest against minimal Express app + `authenticateToken` middleware; mock `pool.execute` for user lookup.

## Validation tests

When changing `server/utils/validation.ts`, update `__tests__/unit/validation.test.ts`:

- Task create requires `status` + `priority` as **int FK IDs**.
- Login/register schema bounds.

## Cache tests

`delKeyFamily` must delete exact key + prefix family — see `cacheInvalidation.test.ts`.

## Writing new integration tests

- Mock DB at `pool.execute` level unless CI has MySQL service.
- Use supertest; avoid booting full Next+Express unless necessary.
- Test: 401 without token, 403 without permission, happy path shape `{ success: true }`.

## Before PR / commit

1. `npm test`
2. `npm run build`
3. Manual smoke for touched flows (see TESTING_SCENARIOS IDs if applicable)

## Do not

- Commit `.env` secrets.
- Skip server-side permission tests when adding new mutations.
- Add tests that depend on production DB without skip guard.
